{"id":91,"date_year":1983,"date_month":"JUL","date_day":15,"artist":"The B‐52s","venue":"Merriweather Post Pavilion","location":"Columbia, MD, USA","details":{"setlistArtist":"The B-52s","setlist":["Song for a Future Generation","Planet Claire","Legal Tender","Big Bird","Whammy Kiss","Butterbean","Dance This Mess Around","Mesopotamia","Private Idaho","Give Me Back My Man","Rock Lobster"],"notes":"Touring heavily behind their third studio album, Whammy! (released April 1983), which pushed the band's sound past its original surf-garage-rock boundaries into drum machines and synthesizers, securing them as regular MTV fixtures. This performance featured the band's original, beloved five-piece lineup — one of the final tours with pioneering guitarist Ricky Wilson, whose distinctively tuned, driving guitar anchored the live show before his death in 1985. The set opened with 'Song for a Future Generation,' the standard tour opener featuring introductions from all five members, and closed with the chaotic, crowd-pleasing 'Rock Lobster.'"}},
