{"id":3,"date_year":1998,"date_month":"SEP","date_day":16,"artist":"Eminem","venue":"Maritime Hall","location":"San Francisco, CA, USA","details":{"headline":"De La Soul, Black Eyed Peas & Eminem","lineup":["De La Soul (headliner)","Black Eyed Peas","Eminem","Ras Kass","The Last Emperor","Rah Sun","Syndicate"],"setlistArtist":"Eminem","setlist":["Scary Movie","My Name Is","Bad Meets Evil","Role Model","Just Don't Give a Fuck"],"notes":"Eminem was low on the bill — a then-unknown, fresh-faced new kid who hadn't yet released The Slim Shady LP — and played a brief, high-energy underground set. Black Eyed Peas were performing their early underground material, long before Fergie joined the group. Wyclef Jean made a surprise appearance to freestyle during the Black Eyed Peas' closing set."}},
